<section id="ai-clients">
  <h2>AI clients</h2>

  <p>
    AI clients like Claude Code read and write <b>your own entries</b> through done's MCP server at
    <code><%= mcp_url %></code>.
  </p>

  <h3>1. Create an access token</h3>
  <p>
    Open <%= link_to "Account → Access tokens", user_access_tokens_path %>. Name the token after where you use it,
    e.g. "Claude Code laptop", pick the orgs or projects it may reach, each with <b>read</b> or <b>read and write</b>,
    and an expiry. Copy the token (<code>done_pat_…</code>): it is shown only once.
  </p>
  <p>
    A token reaches only your own entries, in projects you take part in, and only as long as you do. It has no access
    to settings, members or other people's entries.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Add done to Claude Code</h3>
  <p>For all your projects:</p>
  <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http --scope user done <%= mcp_url %> \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer done_pat_…"</code></pre>
  <p>Or for one repository, without the token in the file, in <code>.mcp.json</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "done": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "<%= mcp_url %>",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${DONE_TOKEN}" }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
  <p>Set <code>DONE_TOKEN</code> in your shell. <code>/mcp</code> in Claude Code shows whether done is connected, and its tools.</p>

  <h3>3. Use it</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>"Which done projects can you see?"</li>
    <li>"Log in acme/website for today: <code>start@9:00 Reviewed the checkout PR #review for~1h30m</code>"</li>
    <li>"Mark my entry about the checkout PR as done."</li>
    <li>"What did I log last week in acme/website, and are there any time issues?"</li>
    <li>"Export my hours for September in acme/website as CSV."</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Claude Code asks before each write unless you allow the tool. Past days stay locked unless you say to change them
    ("yes, change yesterday").
  </p>

  <h3>4. Revoke</h3>
  <p>
    <b>Account → Access tokens → Revoke</b>: the next call fails. Remove the server from Claude Code with
    <code>claude mcp remove done</code>.
  </p>
</section>
